{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.6,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["R88"],
      "pins": ["R88.1", "R88.2"],
      "nets": ["VOUTN", "VOUTP"],
      "observed": "R88 is valued \"24k\" (24 kΩ) in the netlist and the SPICE deck (\"R88 VOUTN VOUTP 24k\"). Its library description says \"24Ω\", and its MPN FRC0805J240TSD encodes 24 Ω (\"240\"). The value field disagrees with the part's own description and MPN.",
      "expected": "R88 should be a 24 Ω part, consistent with its description and MPN, across the VOUTN–VOUTP rail as the design intends.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(comp (ref \"R88\") (value \"24k\") ... (description \" 125mW Thick Film Resistors 150V ±100ppm/℃ ±5% 24Ω 0805 Chip Resistor - Surface Mount ROHS\")"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(property (name \"MPN\") (value \"FRC0805J240TSD\"))"},
        {"source": "spice", "quote": "R88 VOUTN VOUTP 24k"}
      ],
      "impact": "If R88 is really 24 kΩ rather than 24 Ω, the load or balancing path across the VOUTP/VOUTN output is about 1000× higher impedance than intended. That changes the loading and any current-sharing or dummy-load behaviour on the rectified output rail.",
      "confidence": 0.6
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["D7", "D18", "D23"],
      "pins": ["D7.2", "D18.2", "D23.2"],
      "nets": ["/NET0152"],
      "observed": "The anodes of three indicator LEDs (D7, D18, D23) sit on a net, /NET0152, that contains only those three anode pins. No supply, resistor or driver is connected to it. Other indicator LEDs in the same design (e.g. D16, D34) have their anodes on +3V3.",
      "expected": "The anodes of these status LEDs should be tied to +3V3 (or another supply), as the other indicator LEDs are. Their cathodes are driven through current-limit resistors from the Ethernet and PI activity signals.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"32\") (name \"/NET0152\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"D18\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"D23\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"D7\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\")))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"D16\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\"))"}
      ],
      "impact": "With no supply on their anodes, D7, D18 and D23 cannot light. The Ethernet link/activity indications (nLED2, nLED3) and the PI activity indicator are lost, so the board gives no status feedback for those signals.",
      "confidence": 0.35
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The most likely deviation is R88, whose value field reads 24k while its description and MPN specify a 24 Ω part, which would change the output-rail impedance by about 1000×. A less certain second finding is that the anodes of D7, D18 and D23 sit on a net with no supply connection."
}

